### Expected behavior

The certificate chain is validated correctly without any error.

### Actual behavior

Fails with

> Failure PartialChain - unable to get local issuer certificate

### Regression?

Not sure

### Known Workarounds

_No response_

### Configuration

Dotnet: 8.0.100-preview.1.23115.2 
OS: `Linux jborean-linux 6.1.15-200.fc37.x86_64 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Mar  3 17:29:44 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux`

This does not affect Windows, it is able to validate the chain correctly. I have not tested on macOS but if it also uses the same OpenSSL path it will most likely fail there as well.

### Other information

I assume a workaround would be for [OpenSslCertificateAssetDownloader.DownloadCertificate](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/2b185ac8c5c1302804a3336c62cb33782d9d4916/src/libraries/System.Security.Cryptography/src/System/Security/Cryptography/X509Certificates/OpenSslCertificateAssetDownloader.cs#L16-L40) to use `X509Certificate2Collection` which is able to import such a file and handle that as needed. I have no idea how the calling code is meant to handle 2+ certificates though and how it handles cross signed certs which is the case here.
